  "facts": [
    "Completed in 1903, the Williamsburg Bridge was the longest suspension bridge span in the world at 7,308 feet until 1924, showcasing remarkable engineering of its time.",
    "The bridge's main span measures 1,600 feet and is supported by four main cables, suspended from two towering 335-foot structures, a distinctive feature among suspension bridges.",
    "Undergoing significant renovations in the 1980s and 1990s due to severe structural defects, the Williamsburg Bridge continues to be updated, with ongoing work in the 2020s to ensure its longevity."
